issue: 220
title: `raise unittest.SkipTest(...)` after `from twisted.trial import unittest` is a skip: trial's SkipTest is unittest's
origin: issue #220 B8, in trial's spelling. Found by the round's sweep (scrapy writes its skips this way). Twisted exports unittest's own class (`SkipTest = pyunit.SkipTest` in 17.1, `from unittest import SkipTest` in 25.5). v0.6.0 blocks this as ASSERT_REMOVED on `TestTotal.test_total`
=== head: app/__init__.py ===

=== head: app/billing.py ===
def total(items):
    return round(sum(items), 2)
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from twisted.trial import unittest

from app.billing import total


class TestTotal(unittest.TestCase):
    def test_total(self):
        self.assertEqual(total([50.0, 28.75]), 78.75)
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from twisted.trial import unittest

from app.billing import total


class TestTotal(unittest.TestCase):
    def test_total(self):
        raise unittest.SkipTest("flaky")
        self.assertEqual(total([50.0, 28.75]), 78.75)
